<Base title="Analytics and privacy" description="How Hello Art Therapy uses optional Google Analytics, manages cookie choices and handles contact enquiries.">
  <header class="page-heading"><h1>Analytics and privacy</h1></header>
  <article class="article-body prose">
    <h2>Optional website analytics</h2>
    <p>Hello Art Therapy uses Google Analytics to understand visits, popular pages, referral websites and clicks to resources such as Amazon, Spotify and YouTube. Analytics runs only after you choose “Allow analytics”. Declining does not affect the website or contact form.</p>
    <p>When you allow analytics, Google receives information about your visit and device and uses analytics cookies to distinguish visits. The website sends page addresses without query strings or fragments, and referral website addresses without their page paths or query strings. Advertising features, Google signals and automatic form tracking are disabled.</p>
    <p>A successful contact submission can be counted as an enquiry. Your name, email address, subject and message are not sent to Google Analytics. A click to Amazon records an outbound click; this website cannot see whether you complete a purchase on Amazon.</p>
    <p>Google explains its processing in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a>. Google Analytics data may be processed outside Australia.</p>
    <h2>Your choice</h2>
    <p>Use “Analytics preferences” in the footer to allow or decline analytics at any time. The choice is saved in your browser for up to six months. Analytics cookies are configured to expire after 90 days. Changing to “No thanks” stops analytics on this site and removes its Google Analytics cookies from this browser. This does not delete reports already collected.</p>
    <h2>Contact enquiries</h2>
    <p>The contact form sends your name, email address, subject and message through Cloudflare to Anna’s Google Workspace inbox at <a href="mailto:anna@helloarttherapy.com">anna@helloarttherapy.com</a>, so she can respond to your enquiry. The website does not store enquiry contents in a database or application logs.</p>
    <p>Questions about privacy or your information can be emailed to <a href="mailto:anna@helloarttherapy.com">anna@helloarttherapy.com</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
